==Strategy==
Li'l Eraser as the boss is an incredibly dangerous backliner, and being paired with threats like Li'l Bun Bun and Li'l Dark Cat makes for a wicked combo. The One Horns at the start of the stage will give you enough cash to spawn your backliners quickly, though using a [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] is still recommended, as money will be limited later in the stage. Because of this, '''it's important to keep your backliners alive''', because it will be hard to spawn them again.

Playing very close to your Cat Base is recommended, since most units in {{4c}} have rather slow speed and can clog up the cat limit easily.

[[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] will be your main damage dealers in this stage, as very few other {{4c}} units outrange Li'l Dark and deal great damage with Area Attack.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] - Haniwa resists both of the bosses and can survive a Li'l Eraser hit starting at Lv.44. In case you haven't beaten [[An Ancient Curse]], they can also tank a Li'l Eraser hit at Lv.40 with a Defense [[Cat Combo]]. Haniwa is cheap, but also very slow, and may clog the Cat Limit if you are fighting far from your base. They're also very vulnerable to the Li'l Bun Buns and Owlbrows.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] - Stone Cat is a great choice on many stages, but especially so here. The high damage of the Owlbrows, Li'l Bun Buns and Li'l Eraser Cat means nothing to them. As per usual, Research Combos make them even better and are highly recommended.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] - Macho Crystal Cat is a great unit here, as their knockback can potentially save a Mythic Cat that's in danger of being hit, and their slow lasts for a long time. Make sure not to waste them on a B.B.Bunny.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] - Great spammability and DPS, plus is Strong against the Li'l Bun Buns. She can also deal with the One Horns pretty well, but isn't too useful outside of those two enemies. Her slow speed means you should play close to the Cat Base, since she might take a while to get to the frontlines and start attacking Li'l Bun Bun if she's far away.
*[[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]] - Bubble Cat outranges the Owlbrows by a decent margin, and can snipe them with its high piercing range. It's less effective than Cameraman against the Li'l Bun Buns though, due to their fast speed and its large blindspot.
* [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] - As a backliner, Ururun is able to deal constant damage to the bosses. She has the added bonus of [[Knockback]], allowing you to keep pushing the frontline back.
* [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]] - Urs can do the same as Ururun, except with [[Weaken]] instead of Knockback, which is still useful.
*[[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] - She has high piercing range to kill the Owlbrows, decent damage and a fairly quick recharge time for a Legend Cat, making her a great choice here. She can also survive a Li'l Eraser attack at just Lv.30 and has enough range to outrange it too.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] - Jagando has fairly low range for a Legend Cat, but can still be of use. He can use the peons as stepping stones to land [[Surge Attack]]s on Li'l Dark and Li'l Eraser, but be warned, he is very fragile here.
*[[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Mewtone]] - Provides great super-backline damage while also providing valuable CC to One Horn and Li'l Bun Bun.

